\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  O ye sinner be so happy
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj because of your Jesus' sufferings
\par the shedding of His precious blood
\par to shed your tears of thanksgiving
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj show the price that he paid for you
\par seek your life through that same dying
\par Up on His cross only for you
\par you receive peace and happiness.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Look your destruction is too great
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Had it not been Jesus you're dead
\par blind and dead man you are also
\par and you do all the works of sin
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par For by the law you should be killed
\par There is no one to intercede
\par in heaven and here on earth too
\par there is no pardon either too
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. What do you have as an off'ring
\par     With which to pacify your Judge.
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 He who's wearing the crown of thorns
\par God's son he is defending you.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par His tears and wounds all completely
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj To your rescue, come and give thanks.
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Jesus your only Redeemer
\par Has removed all your transgressions.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  When you see the power of your sins
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 and all the chains of your spirit
\par and thus has open up your head
\par and you are nearer to  your grave,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par You dare not say; I have made it!
\par Come to me with all of your chains!
\par Come and see Jesus on the Cross,
\par For Him to break your chains for you.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  He saves sinners from perishing,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 and gives to them aboundant grace!
\par He gives regretfulness and faith
\par He gives them love and also hope
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par He also gives help to the blind,
\par The death and also to cripples.
\par Who ever do here this message,
\par Come with your burden for your grace.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6.  O, my Saviour, I'm so wretched,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 but your grace is bounteous for me;
\par You have redeemed me from my sins,
\par and you saved me from all evil.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par And so Lord, cleanse me from my heart,
\par dwell in me your Holy spirit.
\par Let my spirit, soul and body
\par have your grace and eternal life.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7.  O, my Saviour and my lover,
\par \pard\li315\sl202\slmult0 What again then must I look for?
\par What is so greater than your love
\par to us than your eternal life?
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par If I have Him as my Saviour,
\par there is nothing so to worry;
\par not afraid in death nor in hell
\par \pard        my Saviour is my protector.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

